{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>על עלתך</b> — defective, without vav, for the Holy One, blessed be He, did not desire them. As it says: 'Better a dry morsel and quietness therein than a house full of sacrifices of strife' (Proverbs 17:1) — ר\"ת ממזר, i.e., from the seven bulls and seven rams that the Moabites brought, who came from mamzerut." "<b>יִרְאַנִי</b> — twice. Here and the other: אֱלֹהִים יִרְאַנִי בְשׁוֹרֵרִי. Teaches that Balaam hated them and desired to curse them more than Balak did, and he would pray against them: אֱלֹהִים יִרְאַנִי בְשׁוֹרֵרִי." "<b>וַיֵּלֶךְ שָׁפִי</b> — in gematria חִגֵּר בַּרֶגֶל. Another interpretation: from the root שׁוּף, 'crush,' מִדּוּכְתֵּיהּ, because it says: 'and pressed Balaam's foot against the wall' (Numbers 22:25)." "<b>שָׁפִי</b> — pe alef doubled (כפולה). He scrutinized and searched for which hour was propitious to curse Israel."], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:22:59.084220182Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}